{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Self::NodeId>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`. This rests on the supplied test sources and a quick look at the trait declarations in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. An application domain implements `Domain`, with the declared associated types and methods (`node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`).\n2. `Domain` is `Clone + Send + Sync`, so a domain is cloneable and safe to share between executions.\n3. `NodeId` is `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. `EdgeLabel` is `Clone + Send + Sync`. `Error` is only `Send`. `NodeContent` is `NodeContents`.\n4. The `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures are `Send`.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` is the main contract test.\n  - It implements `Domain` for a fixture with opaque types: an `Identity` that is `Clone + Eq`, a `Label` that is only `Clone`, and a `GraphError` that is `Send` but not `Sync`, `Debug`, `Clone` or `Error`. This shows the trait does not demand extra bounds.\n  - The generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` function requires `Clone + Send + Sync` on `G`, `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync` on `NodeId`, `Clone + Send + Sync` on `EdgeLabel`, `Send` on `Error`, and `NodeContents + Send + Sync` on `NodeContent`. If any declared bound were loosened, this would fail to compile.\n  - The fixture's non-`Sync` error confirms the load and store futures stay `Send` without a `Sync` error. `check_bounds` and the awaited `send(...)` calls both pin this.\n  - It calls every member and asserts the results.\n    - `node_content` returns content whose `format()` and `fingerprint().value` are both \"1\".\n    - `load_evidence` returns `None`.\n    - `store_evidence` returns `Ok`.\n    - `node_path` returns the expected segments and differs between nodes.\n    - `outgoing_edges` returns the expected lists, including duplicates and order. An unknown label and a node with no edges both return an empty list. The error case returns the application's own error.\n- Further tests cover \"safe to share between executions\", with domains cloned and used concurrently:\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`\n  \n  The first two run concurrent validations against one domain, and the last runs two same-criterion executions concurrently.\n- Other marked tests use real `Domain` implementations end to end, with assertions on the stored and loaded records:\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]`\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` covers the SDK's own domain contents.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. The `NodeContent` bound is `NodeContents`, which `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[NodeContents]` declares as `Send + Sync`. The `Send + Sync` check on `NodeContent` in `check_bounds` is therefore consistent with the requirement text.",
  "references": "e4523d0723dbae733a91c6ba03e29b0b84d9d7c718e69c4e9151d82f33785a6b",
